  {
    "id": "cvpr26-cad19a2921a3",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-cad19a2921a3",
      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4. Overview of generalist reward model. Left: Given a before-edited image and a user-edited after image After-u (â€œuâ€ for â€œuserâ€), we perturb the editing process to obtain a suboptimal image, After-w (â€œwâ€ for â€œweakâ€). Middle: In the SFT stage,the reward model ï¬rst learns to generate metrics and then produces scalar rewards for the two input images. Right: In the RL stage, we introduce policy-guided reward training (PGRT), where the suboptimal image After-w is provided by the policy model rather than generated through perturbation. The goal of the RL stage is to assign a higher scalar reward to the user-edited (strong) image After-u.",
      "page": 5,
