      "id": "cvpr26-c241eb5a89d8",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the InstantViR framework. (Top) Training: We train a single-step solver qÏ• using only degraded measurements y. The solver is optimized with two objectives: a data fidelity loss (ensuring the reconstruction matches the measurement y) and a prior distillation loss (using a frozen video diffusion prior [24], sÎ¸, to enforce temporal consistency and realism). (Bottom) Inference: The trained solver qÏ• operates as a fast, feed-forward network, processing the video in a causal, block-wise, and autoregressive manner. This enables real-time, single-step streaming reconstruction with optional text guidance.",
      "page": 5,
