      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the Adaptive Text Dreamer (ATD) architecture. The dual-branch weight-sharing leftâ€“right vision-language model (VLM) structure consists of a left-brain branch that performs state estimation using a large language model (LLM), and a right-brain branch that generates future candidate imaginations constrained by latent embeddings derived from the state estimation. The imagined latent representations are then integrated into a graph-based navigation expert to guide action decisions.",
